# Local iterate, then ship on request

Default for package / UI / functionality work: change code, apply it on
**this** FosOS install, and leave Version / git / APT alone until the user
explicitly asks to bump, commit, push, or publish.

## While iterating (default)

- Do **not** change `Version:` in any `packages/*/DEBIAN/control`
- Do **not** commit, push, run APT publish/promote, or build an ISO unless
  the user asks
- After edits under `packages/`, rebuild the touched package(s) with
  `scripts/stage-deb.sh` / `stage_deb` at the **current** version and
  reinstall with `sudo dpkg -i` (same-version reinstall is intentional)
- Restart what the change needs so the user can judge it: desktop shell /
  panel for `fosos-desktop` UI; greeter restart for greeter-only; reboot
  for Plymouth / GRUB / theme boot path
- Keep working this way across many small changes until they say they are
  satisfied

## When the user asks to ship

Only then, in the order they request (typical: bump → commit → push →
publish testing):

1. Bump `Version:` only for packages that actually changed in the batch
2. Commit (and push) when asked
3. Publish to **testing** when asked (Actions → APT publish, or
   `sudo bash scripts/apt-archive.sh publish`)

Still give the ISO vs APT delivery warning from `iso-vs-apt-warn` for what
changed. Live-image / `build/live-build/` work cannot be hot-installed; say
so and do not pretend a local `.deb` reinstall covers it.

## Do not

- Bump versions “to be safe” before each local install
- Publish or promote because a local apply succeeded
- Assume satisfaction; wait for an explicit ship request
